 and  have it be like trigger plus one of the  face buttons  because then you have way more control  which reminds me  reviving a downed player requires you to  press  r2 and l1 at the same time  why not l1 and r1 why not r2 and l2  why that why the most awkward possible  combination of buttons  every individual turtle carries their  own items you can get pickups like pizza  for health packs  throwing stars and grenades cause we  know how much the ninja turtles love  grenades  and that works fine for multiplayer  whoever picks it up should be the one to  use it  but in single player these items don't  transfer when you switch characters mid  gameplay  i could have stocked up on health and  weapons leonardo  gotten overwhelmed by enemies and  knocked out and then have none of that  stuff as any of the other three turtles  with no way to revive him because  reviving players costs a health pick up  except for special occasions where it  randomly doesn't for some reason  boss fights don't have health bars  either and just do like 80  unblockable attacks so you have to just  take the hit because ranged combat is  practically non-existent  thankfully there really aren't that many  bosses in the game anyway  you fight karai twice baxter stockman's  robot  and shredder twice the real difficulty  for all of these comes from just braving  the overwhelming  constant waves of enemies that all feel  just  as tough individually as the boss is  there anything i like about this game  you may ask  well i i like the designs for the  turtles this is a really decent take on  them in a realistic art style and i  wish they look more like this in the  movies instead of the 9 foot tall shreks  covered with over designed garbage  and um the way you climb up  stuff looks cool can we talk about the  bugs let's talk about the bugs there's  this part of the docks where you're  climbing around on shipping containers  but baxter stockman springs a trap where  he blocks the way he came in and a bunch  of enemies attack you while he watches  from a security camera perspective  that's fine these types of games do  things like that all the time but the  game bugged out in this spot for me  because i could still climb on the boxes  and go back over the barricade where i  came from  where i found out that they called out  half the level and i could walk out of  bounds  then i went back to the intended area to  go forward and it repeated the security  camera fight again  only this time it wouldn't end after i  beat all the enemies so i go and hack  the door twice to get through it because  this game's broken  and then the door closes behind me and  then calls out the rest of the level  so now i'm just stuck staring at a wall  i figured out i could switch  turtles to make the camera quickly  teleport over but still had this dumb  static camera filter over it and it  wouldn't go away no matter what i did  so i proceed to do the next fight scene  where i get my shell handed to me and i  get sent back to the previous area to do  the security camera part again  and it's broken in the same way every  time now  it took me like six tries to finally get  through this area  because the checkpoint was so  unforgiving and every time it had this  stupid camera filter  because that was the only way i could  progress in fact all of these  checkpoints are really  unforgiving other times i've had prompts  that wouldn't go away even after i  pressed them  i fell out of the map during the final  boss and of course the camera's just  always buggy and just sticks in walls  and i can't see anything  i read that the ps3 version i'm playing  came out almost a year after the xbox  version to iron out some of the bugs and  polish it up  so i can only imagine how broken that  port was  this is the fixed one and last because  of the silent reaper that is copyright  licensing  this game was delisted from all digital  stores everywhere in 2017.  i can't say i'm too heartbroken over the  law so that i wish more people had  gotten a chance to play it  it's not an underrated hidden gem or  anything people with like  another year or two of testing and  polishing it would have been at least  kind of mediocre but i hate that  superhero games can all become  so hard to come by after a certain time  period makes me think that i just need  to buy  any and all games featuring a comic book  character as quickly as possible before  they're gone forever like a fortnight  skin punisher no mercy unplayable  marvel heroes online gone forever any  spider-man game before the current one  ultimate alliance on next-gen deadpool  all can't be purchased digitally anymore  you have to find a disk and those are  becoming rarer by the day  for the sake of preservation this is why  emulation is a godsend  though even that has its faults because  i couldn't emulate either of these games  as long as the files for them are out  there these games can still be  appreciated forever  good or bad these games are part of tmnt  history  don't deserve to be lost forever if you  somehow find a way to play them  go ahead if you're a turtles fan  whatever you have done extremely well my  sons  you have persevered against great  challenges and hardships  i am proud of you yeah we also gave  shredder a good  beating yes that is good too  celebrate and rest now  but the battle is not over  yo donny big brains  okay there forget outdoors work fellas  [Music]  you
 

